# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Cygwin/Git-bash crash dumps (e.g. du.exe.stackdump)
*.stackdump

# Added by cargo

/target
# Isolated build dir used to compile/iterate while a long background run holds a
# file-lock on target/release/*.exe on Windows (see code_report.md / CLAUDE.md).
/target-*/
/target-test-build.log
/prompts

# Regenerable curated exports derived from the committed label corpus
# (data/label_corpus/.../images.jsonl) — not source, not committed.
/beautiful_locations.json

# Python palette-library prototype: harvested third-party .ugr/.map collections
# are local working inputs only — never redistribute (see palette_lib/REPORT.md).
# The colormap-derived palette library (clean/quarantined/log) IS committed; see
# the /data negations below.
/palette_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Python uv environment (see CLAUDE.md "Python / uv"). The venv is regenerable
# from pyproject.toml + uv.lock via `uv sync` — both of those ARE committed.
/.venv/

# All generated artifacts live under the single scratch/ tree (see CLAUDE.md,
# "Generated-output convention"). Ignore the whole tree but keep its anchor so
# the directory survives a clean checkout. This blanket rule subsumes the old
# per-dir/per-file entries (/renders, /descend_strip_panels, *_stdout.txt, …).
/scratch/*
!/scratch/.gitkeep
# scratchpad/ is the canonical disposable temp dir (see CLAUDE.md disk-hygiene). It is
# gitignored and MUST never be on anyone's dependency path: nothing outside it imports it,
# and it is never the sole producer of a durable artifact. Load-bearing code -> tools/,
# findings text -> docs/findings/. (The 2026-07-15 promotion pass made this true; a file
# that broke — visual_dup/embed.py — is why this rule exists.)
/scratchpad/
# data/ is disposable by default, EXCEPT the committed colormap-derived palette
# library (reproducible from palette_lib/build_sheet.py — see CLAUDE.md
# "Persistent-store convention").
#
# NOTE (storage restructure): regenerable file-count bombs are RELOCATED out of the
# tree to ARTIFACTS_ROOT (default sibling ../fractal-maker-artifacts, env
# FRACTAL_ARTIFACTS_ROOT); readers/writers route through tools/corpus/artifacts.py.
# Two families: the LIVE data/v8/aug_cache (a literal in RELOCATED_PREFIXES; the
# v4..v7 caches were deleted and their literals dropped), and the discovery-scratch
# CLASS — any data/discovery/**/scratch tree — matched by pattern, so a new campaign
# relocates with no registry edit (steered_frontier.py declares it bulk() at its write
# site). campaign2 breadth/dive scratch (317k files / ~45 GB) was reclaimed. No
# .gitignore lines are dead: these families were only ever ignored by the blanket
# `/data/*` and `/data/discovery/**/scratch/` rules below, which remain load-bearing
# for OTHER in-tree paths and also serve as a backstop (any accidental in-tree rebuild
# stays un-committable).
/data/*
# Durable minibrot roster (tools/sourcing/build_minibrot_roster.py): records a per-
# (degree,band) atom selection + a train/eval split that later descent crops inherit.
# Impossible to reproduce identically across future sourcing runs -> committed by path.
!/data/minibrot_roster/
# (No negation for /data/q4_stage1/ — deliberately.) The q4 stage-1 label-set fields were
# tracked as DURABLE on 2026-08-04 and DELETED BY DECISION the same day. The durability
# verdict was wrong: it re-dumped through the `beautiful` kernel (default bailout 2^16) and
# read the resulting +3.4712 offset as irreproducibility, but the writer those fields
# actually come from is `--dump-field-source f64`, which reproduces them BYTE-IDENTICALLY
# (sha256 equal on 4/4 spot-checked, ~1.7 s each). They are bulk-regenerable, so they are
# gitignored like the rest of /data/*; `LS.FIELDS` goes through paths.bulk(). Rebuild with
# `uv run python tools/studies/q4_multibrot_transfer.py corpus-fields` (~60 s for all 33).
# Minibrot descent harness (tools/descent/, prompts/descent_harness_build.md +
# prompts/minibrot_triage_wall.md): the durable human records — selection subset,
# per-emit solution lineages, verified-bad verdicts, and the triage wall's
# accept/reject verdicts + its atom pool — are irreplaceable choices, committed by
# exact path. The IMAGE families (emitted canonical+vivid crop pairs, triage-wall
# thumbnails) are regenerable bulk that relocates OUT of the tree via
# tools/corpus/artifacts.resolve (like every other corpus crop) —
# artifacts._is_descent_harness_crop still names {crops,vivid,thumbs} explicitly on the
# resolver side. (Nav previews live in scratch/.)
#
# WALK-DOWN, not a directory negation. This stanza used to be `!/data/descent_harness/`
# with the three bulk dirs re-ignored beneath it, which inverts the default for
# everything ELSE: a family that did not exist when those three lines were written —
# previews/, triage/tiles/, anything a later harness adds — was committable the moment
# it appeared, and nothing here would have said so. Same shape as the palettes and
# label_corpus stanzas: un-ignore the directory so git descends, re-exclude its
# contents, then re-include the durable records by exact path. Adding a record now
# takes a line here, which is the point.
!/data/descent_harness/
/data/descent_harness/*
!/data/descent_harness/selection.json
!/data/descent_harness/selection_triage.json
!/data/descent_harness/emits.jsonl
!/data/descent_harness/verified_bad.json
!/data/descent_harness/triage/
/data/descent_harness/triage/*
!/data/descent_harness/triage/enum_state.json
!/data/descent_harness/triage/neighbors.json
!/data/descent_harness/triage/pool.jsonl
!/data/descent_harness/triage/references.json
!/data/descent_harness/triage/verdicts.jsonl
# Minibrot source sheets (tools/sources/, prompts/minibrot_source_sheets.md): the
# nuclei lists + descriptors are a durable computed population everything downstream
# keys off, committed by exact path. The rendered tiles and the sheet HTML are
# regenerable-but-expensive bulk that relocates OUT of the tree via
# tools/corpus/artifacts.resolve (artifacts._is_minibrot_source_bulk), so their dirs
# are re-ignored below.
!/data/minibrot_sources/
/data/minibrot_sources/tiles/
/data/minibrot_sources/sheets/
# Newton divergence-abort parity table (tools/sourcing/newton_parity.py): the pinned
# outcome of the PRE-ABORT reference solver over the two slow-lane roster grids. ~1 MB of
# text, it is an INPUT to test_newton_divergence_abort.py, and re-deriving it was 80.6% of
# the whole `slow` lane -> durable, committed by exact path.
!/data/sourcing/
/data/sourcing/*
!/data/sourcing/newton_parity_ref.json
# Orbital-falloff measures (tools/orbital/, prompts/orbital_falloff_criterion.md):
# per-atom field metrics keyed by the shared content-hash atom id, plus the maxiter
# stability check and the validation outcome. Small, load-bearing text -> committed.
!/data/orbital/
!/data/palettes/
/data/palettes/*
!/data/palettes/clean_colormaps.json
!/data/palettes/quarantined_colormaps.json
!/data/palettes/quarantine_log.json
# durable palette trajectory-feature file (tools/palettes/build_features.py):
# reproducible but load-bearing -- downstream samplers/dispatch load it directly.
!/data/palettes/score3_colormaps.json
!/data/palettes/palette_features.json
# durable merged palette pool (tools/palettes/build_pool.py): the preference
# network's palette source of truth (curated q2/q3 + quality-passing extracted).
!/data/palettes/pool_colormaps.json
# durable palette color-axis categorization (tools/palettes/build_categories.py):
# one hierarchical tree cut at k=8/12/16, nested; special cells + stored linkage.
!/data/palettes/palette_categories.json
# vivid blue/orange companion map (the roster pilot sheet's _blue_orange, baked as a
# render-one colormap library): the label-crop vivid companions rebuild from it — durable.
!/data/palettes/vivid_blue_orange.json
# The levels reference (tools/palettes/levels_reference.py): the tone-statistic band the
# production auto-level projects onto, read off Matt's read-only LevelsCheck folder. That
# folder lives OUTSIDE the repo, so nothing here rebuilds an earlier band — durable, and a
# tracked canary (tests/test_tracked_artifacts.py).
!/data/palettes/levels_reference.json
# The auto-level ADOPTION record (tools/palettes/adopt_autolevel.py): the 2026-08-11 flip of
# the operator's switch -- date, evidence, what it does not touch, how to revert. Regenerable
# from the live modules by design, and durable because a decision is not a derived artifact.
!/data/palettes/autolevel_adoption.json
# Hand-picked reference test fixtures (load-bearing metadata, not regenerable):
# the test render locations and the test palette selection.
!/data/test_renders.json
!/data/test_palettes.json
# Emission-v1 diversity target measure (tools/emission): a hand-editable config that is
# part of the deficit definition, not a regenerable artifact — commit it.
!/data/emission/
!/data/emission/target_measure.json
# The relit library look-seed's per-medoid CLIP vectors: bulk, resolved OUT of the tree by
# artifacts.RELOCATED_PREFIXES. `!/data/emission/` above re-includes this subtree, so an
# in-tree straggler would be COMMITTED rather than merely present — this stanza is the
# belt-and-braces half for a writer that bypassed the resolver. The snapshot beside it
# (library_seed_v2/intake.json) stays tracked: it is durable, and not under `embs/`.
/data/emission/library_seed_v2/embs/
# v3's per-medoid vectors: same class, same stanza. Written 2026-08-10 by
# production_run_25's post-run seed repopulation (v2's 168 human->=3 looks UNIONED with the
# run's emission intake, v2 winning every collision). The snapshot beside it
# (library_seed_v3/intake.json + morph_embs.npz) stays tracked for the same reason v2's does.
/data/emission/library_seed_v3/embs/
# campaign1's per-medoid vectors: same class, same stanza. The family is dark (its
# snapshot was never rebuilt after the derived-artifact wipe); the rule exists so a relight
# cannot commit 168+ vectors by default.
/data/emission/campaign1/embs/
# Permanent label corpus (see data/label_corpus/CORPUS_SCHEMA.md): commit the
# tiny, irreplaceable metadata (schema, batch.json, images.jsonl, scores.json);
# gitignore crops/ — each crop is a pure function of its row's `render` block,
# rebuildable via render-one.
!/data/label_corpus/
/data/label_corpus/batches/*/crops/
# vivid (blue/orange) companion crops — the labeler-judges-from render; rebuildable
# from the row's render block under a vivid palette, same policy as crops/.
/data/label_corpus/batches/*/vivid/
# Wallpaper-quality corpus (tools/wallpaper/build_bootstrap.py) — same policy: commit
# batch.json + images.jsonl + scores.json, gitignore the rebuildable crops.
!/data/wallpaper_corpus/
/data/wallpaper_corpus/batches/*/crops/
# q4 window label store (tools/studies/q4_stage1_labelset.py; schema
# data/q4_window_corpus/README.md) — same policy: commit windows.jsonl + meta.json +
# README + scores.json, gitignore the crops (rebuildable: re-dump the field then
# colorize+crop via the capture stage).
!/data/q4_window_corpus/
/data/q4_window_corpus/batches/*/crops/
# Render-mode ("mining") corpus (tools/mining/build_mining_sheet.py) — the ONE label
# corpus in this repo that had NO negation, which is exactly why the July pilot+scale
# labels were unjoinable after the wipe (scratch/stage2_label_audit/report.md,
# durability_map.py). Same policy as the three above: commit gate_passers_v3.json +
# batch.json + images.jsonl, gitignore the rebuildable crops and the resume ledger.
!/data/render_mode_corpus/
/data/render_mode_corpus/batches/*/crops/
/data/render_mode_corpus/batches/*/_fields/
/data/render_mode_corpus/batches/*/_progress_ledger.jsonl
# the render stage's hand-off to the write stage; the DURABLE copy of the same failures is
# batch.json's `render_failures`, so tracking both is two owners for one record.
/data/render_mode_corpus/batches/*/_render_errors.json
# disposable per-batch working data (previews, guided-descend pools, intermediate
# scores) — rebuildable from the committed metadata + generator, never committed.
/data/label_corpus/batches/*/_work/
# regenerable view (rev4_sanity_sheet.py) — not part of the commit policy.
/data/label_corpus/batches/*/sanity_contact_sheet.html

# Palette-preference query labels (tools/queries/launch_query_label_server.py):
# the authoritative per-batch hand-labeled tier store is tiny + irreplaceable, so
# commit it; the query batch (records/images) and stamped *_export_* dumps are
# regenerable and stay ignored.
!/data/queries/
/data/queries/*
!/data/queries/labels/
/data/queries/labels/*
!/data/queries/labels/coldstart_v2.json
!/data/queries/labels/warmstart_v1.json
!/data/queries/labels/prefv2_dramatic_v1.json
# sample_location.py eval pools: the runs were unseeded (GPU scoring is
# nondeterministic), so records.json (exact re-renderable configs of the validated
# top-18 pools) + summary.json are NON-regenerable — commit them. The .png sheets
# ARE regenerable (sample_location.py --rebuild-sheets), so they stay ignored.
!/data/queries/sampler_eval/
/data/queries/sampler_eval/*
!/data/queries/sampler_eval/summary.json
!/data/queries/sampler_eval/*/
/data/queries/sampler_eval/*/*
!/data/queries/sampler_eval/*/records.json
# The palette-preference RANKER weight (pref-v3-gvo), `tools/queries/scorer/*`. It was
# tracked by `git add -f` at a gitignored path from the repo import until 2026-08-08 —
# which works, and leaves nothing saying it belongs: a fresh clone's `git add -A` would
# not re-add it, `paths.durable()` REFUSED it and every new sibling, and nothing goes red
# if it silently drops out. A negation is a RULE where a force-add is an EVENT. Exact path,
# never the directory: v3_gvo also holds untracked training state, and a bare
# `!/data/queries/scorer/v3_gvo/` would sweep it in.
!/data/queries/scorer/
/data/queries/scorer/*
!/data/queries/scorer/v3_gvo/
/data/queries/scorer/v3_gvo/*
!/data/queries/scorer/v3_gvo/model_best.pt

# Mandelbrot seed atlas (tools/atlas/build_atlas.py): the fitted theta_hat/conf
# artifact is a tiny (~12KB) load-bearing object the proposer reloads (atlas.py) --
# commit it like the calibration artifacts. Its round0 viz PNGs stay in scratch/.
!/data/atlas/
# ...but NOT the tau_h re-derivation work dir: bulk (a literal in RELOCATED_PREFIXES),
# so tools/atlas/tau_h_rederive.py resolves it OUT of the tree. This rule is the
# belt-and-braces half — without it, the `!/data/atlas/` re-include above would COMMIT
# rows.jsonl and any straggler tile if a writer ever bypassed the resolver.
/data/atlas/tau_h_rederive/

# Production discovery seeder ledgers (tools/atlas/production_seeder.py): the durable
# cross-run outcome/cell ledgers + per-outcome features + per-run summaries are
# load-bearing (the harvested-outcome store everything downstream consumes), committed
# like the atlas. Render scratch (contact_sheet.png review views) is disposable and
# lives under scratch/ (SHEETS_DIR) — never here; the rule below evicts any straggler.
!/data/discovery/
/data/discovery/**/contact_sheet.png
# The steered/dive frontier machinery (steered_frontier.py) adds disposable run
# output beside the durable ledgers: per-node render scratch (cheap JPGs, field
# dumps, expand/nodes logs, pool sheets) and regenerable run-internal state
# (novelty memory, node embeddings, frontier/dive state, prio/saturation
# logs) — crash-safety is by ledger-rebuild, so none of it is source. Only the
# durable harvested-outcome store (outcome_ledger/outcome_feats/probe_rejects/
# guard_telemetry/summary/walks/pool) is committed, matching the seeder above.
# EXCEPTION: harvest_log.jsonl is NOT regenerable and IS committed — it is the sole
# record of every harvest check's (partition, cheap_pgood, canonical fate) triple,
# incl. the canon-not-q3 / precanon-dup REJECTS. The ledger keeps admissions only, so
# rebuilding harvest_log would require re-running the cheap scorer AND the canonical
# render+decode over every candidate (a full re-derivation, not a ledger replay). It
# is the tau_h curve's data on record; ignoring it lost campaign1/2's — see
# docs/design/discovery_pipeline.md §"tau_h on record".
# The STOP sentinel is a CONTROL SIGNAL, not a run artifact — an empty file whose only
# meaning is "halt at the next batch boundary". It was deleted from the tree once
# (58bec40) without a rule to stop it coming back, and it came back.
/data/discovery/**/STOP
/data/discovery/**/scratch/
# The outcome-FEATURE store — demoted from committed to bulk() on 2026-08-08 and moved
# out-of-tree (artifacts._is_discovery_feats). It is the derived sidecar of
# outcome_ledger.jsonl: one 1280-D penultimate vector per admitted q3, recomputable from
# the ledger's own coordinates by re-rendering and re-embedding. The ledger STAYS
# committed — it records a population that cannot be re-walked and carries the label
# provenance — and this does not. Measured before the move: 10.88 MB across 27 banked
# runs, and 3.23 of steady_state_v2_20260807's 10.77 MB of tree bytes, i.e. 30% of a
# modern run's committed footprint for a store production_seeder.py itself describes as
# "logged, never gates". The `_v7_t45` re-decode subset (redecode_grid.py) is the same
# class and matched by the same prefix. The existing files were MOVED, not deleted: a
# recompute embeds through the head active TODAY, and each banked vector was pulled
# through the head named by its own ledger row's scorer_version.
/data/discovery/**/outcome_feats*.npz
/data/discovery/**/*.log
/data/discovery/**/morph_mem.npz
/data/discovery/**/morph_admissions.npz
/data/discovery/**/dive_admissions.npz
/data/discovery/**/node_embs.npz
/data/discovery/**/state.json
/data/discovery/**/dive_state.json
/data/discovery/**/dive_log.jsonl
# EXCEPTION: prio_terms.jsonl is NOT regenerable and IS committed (via LFS) — it is the
# sole record of every PUSHED candidate incl. the never-admitted majority, each with its
# steering score (eord/gumbel/priority + dedup/novelty penalties). It is the steering-side
# counterpart to harvest_log's confirmation-side triple: harvest_log records what happened
# to checks that cleared tau_h; prio_terms records the whole priority-queue population that
# tau_h/scheduling selected FROM. Rebuilding it would require re-running the walk. Recovered
# from a filesystem backup of the old working tree — see docs/design/discovery_pipeline.md
# §"tau_h on record". (Large: ~57-63 MB for the campaign breadth runs → LFS via .gitattributes.)
/data/discovery/**/saturation.jsonl
# Regenerable per-run overlays with no durable consumer: the deficit-scheduler decision
# trace, the within-run morph-embedding/dedup matrix, and the julia-hook seed-injection log
# (kin to node_embs/morph_mem above — rebuildable from the ledger + generator, never source).
/data/discovery/**/scheduler_trace.jsonl
# The v1.5 run-local VIEW-FIELD store (tools/atlas/view_field_cache.RunFieldCache). It is
# the one thing a maneuver run writes that is BULK and REGENERABLE at once: raw 64x36 f32
# fields, ~9 KB a row and hundreds of MB a run, and a deterministic function of the run's
# own maneuvers.jsonl (which IS committed) plus committed code and the stamped cap policy.
# Nothing may depend on it surviving. Ignoring it by DIRECTORY and not by filename because
# the store is three files that must move together — a half-committed cache is worse than
# no cache, since `index.json` would then claim rows `fields.f32` does not hold.
/data/discovery/**/view_fields/
# ...and the crawl's stderr sidecar, which is the `*.log` rule's twin (a detached launch
# splits the two streams; only the log half was covered).
/data/discovery/**/*.err
/data/discovery/**/launch.txt
/data/discovery/**/distinct_looks.npz
/data/discovery/**/julia_hooks.jsonl

# Phase-1 prospect location LIBRARY (written by tools/wallpaper/library_annotate.py; the
# prospect_orchestrator that drove it was deleted 2026-08-10, the store was not). The
# durable records + the consolidated embeddings matrix are load-bearing and
# committed by EXACT PATH — not by directory. A bare `!/data/library_embeddings/`
# would re-include the per-cycle shards/*.npz stream, which is a regenerable overlay
# (consolidated into embeddings.npz) and MUST stay ignored. So: re-include the dir,
# re-exclude its contents, then negate only the one durable file.
!/data/library/
/data/library/*
!/data/library/library_records.jsonl
!/data/library_embeddings/
# The supply crawl's DRAW RECORD and FEATURE TABLE (2026-08-01,
# tools/atlas/build_supply_crawl_batches.py). Small (hundreds of rows), and durable for the
# reason `harvest_log.jsonl` is: the feature table is the join between a label that has not
# been collected yet and the screen measures the candidate carried when it was drawn, keyed
# on the `image_id` the labels will come back under. Re-deriving it later means re-deriving
# the draw, and the draw is seeded off a population that lives in a run dir nothing promises
# to keep. `paths.durable()` refuses to write here without this negation, which is how the
# omission was caught rather than silently discarded.
!/data/supply_crawl/
# The label-seeded harvest's SEED POOL, DRAW RECORD and FEATURE TABLE (2026-08-02,
# tools/atlas/{label_seeded_harvest,build_label_seeded_batches}.py). Durable for the supply
# crawl's reason above, plus one this harvest adds: the seed pool is a snapshot of which
# corpus locations resolved to >= 3 ON THIS DATE, through the amendment overlay as it stood.
# The overlay moves — the 2026-07-28 revisit pass alone promoted 338 rows and demoted 5 — so
# re-deriving the pool later reconstructs a DIFFERENT population and silently re-labels what
# this harvest was seeded from. The record keeps what was true when written
# (`storage_classes.md`).
!/data/label_seeded_harvest/
/data/library_embeddings/*
!/data/library_embeddings/embeddings.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v8 classifier build — DURABLE by exact path.
#
# v4..v7 wrote their manifest/plan/cache_manifest to an ignored, untracked path and
# every one of them is now GONE (see tools/audit/durability_map.py). data/v8/manifest
# .jsonl IS the training population and its train/eval split — every v8 metric is
# quoted against it and it cannot be rebuilt once the live label overlay moves on;
# eval_slice.jsonl is the frozen instrument the v7 comparison runs on. So v8 declares
# these `paths.durable()` and they are re-included here BY EXACT PATH, not by
# directory: a bare `!/data/v8/` would also re-include an accidental in-tree
# aug_cache/ rebuild, which is the one thing that must never land in the tree.
# Enforced: tools/paths.durable() asserts non-ignored at the write site,
# tests/test_tracked_artifacts.py canaries them, .gitattributes routes the big two
# through LFS.
!/data/v8/
/data/v8/*
!/data/v8/manifest.jsonl
!/data/v8/build_metadata.json
!/data/v8/eval_slice.jsonl
# NOT here, and deliberately: plan.jsonl + cache_manifest.jsonl were DELETED 2026-08-03.
# 146 MB of derived rows that `uv run python tools/v8/build_plan.py` reproduces
# BYTE-IDENTICALLY from the committed manifest + colormap sources (proved by rebuild +
# sha256 in that pass, for all four of plan/cache_manifest/colormaps/aug_roster). The
# negation goes with the file: a negation left behind declares durable a path nothing
# writes, and the tracked-artifact canary would then trip on a file that is correctly gone.
# AND SO DOES THE CLASS: build_plan.py writes the pair through paths.bulk(), not durable().
# durable() asserts its target is not ignored, so while the two disagreed the rebuild that
# justifies this deletion raised DurabilityError and never reached its own output.
!/data/v8/aug_roster.json
# The merged render library the cache tiles were actually coloured through. It is a
# verbatim concatenation of two committed sources, so it is cheap to rebuild — but a
# plan row names a palette and NOTHING else records which stops that name resolved to,
# so if either source is ever edited the cache becomes unattributable in exactly the way
# the v4..v7 caches were. Committed for that reason.
!/data/v8/colormaps.json
# v8 EVAL products — DURABLE by exact path. eval_scores_v8.jsonl is the frozen per-location
# eval slice the keeper cut is recut against; the previous slice's NON-durability is the whole
# reason a provenance stamp had to be nulled (data/v7/t_good_derivation.json was cleared and
# gone). eval_results_v8.json is the acceptance battery; t_good_derivation.json is the derived
# per-partition threshold report. Committed so none can be silently regenerated or wiped.
!/data/v8/eval_scores_v8.jsonl
!/data/v8/eval_results_v8.json
!/data/v8/t_good_derivation.json
# Backstop only — the v8 aug cache is bulk() and resolves out-of-tree through
# artifacts.RELOCATED_PREFIXES. If it ever reappears here it stays un-committable.
/data/v8/aug_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v9 classifier build — DURABLE by exact path, same discipline as v8 above.
#
# v9 is the v8 corpus RE-RENDERED at the raised iteration cap
# (docs/design/auto_maxiter.md): same manifest, same split, same loc_ids, same 24-slot
# recipe — only the cap moved, and it moved from a flat 8000 to the per-row production
# policy. It has no manifest.jsonl or eval_slice.jsonl of its own ON PURPOSE: it reads
# v8's, and build_metadata.json records that file's sha256, so "same corpus" is a
# checked claim rather than a duplicated file that can drift.
#
# Re-included BY EXACT PATH, not by directory, for the v8 reason: a bare `!/data/v9/`
# would also re-include an accidental in-tree aug_cache/ rebuild.
#   v9's plan.jsonl + cache_manifest.jsonl had negations here (and LFS rules in
#   .gitattributes) until 2026-08-08, when both were deleted: 146 MB of rows that
#   `tools/v9/build_plan.py` reproduces BYTE-IDENTICALLY from data/v8/manifest.jsonl plus
#   the committed colormap sources (proved by rebuilding over the originals and comparing
#   sha256, 2026-08-08). They were tracked to arm the v10 recipe-parity gate; that gate was
#   retired the same day with the two aug-cache trees it protected. The pair is bulk() now
#   — deliberately untracked, byte-reproducible, and NOT a RELOCATED_PREFIXES entry, so it
#   resolves in-tree at the same path every reader already opens.
!/data/v9/
/data/v9/*
!/data/v9/build_metadata.json
!/data/v9/aug_roster.json
# The merged render library the v9 tiles were coloured through — asserted byte-identical
# to v8's at build time, but committed anyway for v8's reason: a plan row names a palette
# and nothing else records which stops that name resolved to.
!/data/v9/colormaps.json
# v9 EVAL products — the frozen per-location eval slice the keeper cut is recut against,
# the acceptance battery, and the derived per-partition threshold report.
!/data/v9/eval_scores_v9.jsonl
!/data/v9/eval_results_v9.json
!/data/v9/t_good_derivation.json
# Backstop only — the v9 aug cache is bulk() and resolves out-of-tree through
# artifacts.RELOCATED_PREFIXES. If it ever reappears here it stays un-committable.
/data/v9/aug_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v10 classifier build — DURABLE by exact path, same discipline as v8/v9 above.
#
# v10 is an APPEND onto v8's manifest: 1,267 maneuver-view locations from the 2026-08
# supply crawl and the label-seeded harvest, on top of v8's byte-frozen 7,115-row prefix
# (tools/v10/build_manifest.py GATE 11). Unlike v9 it DOES have a manifest and an
# eval_slice of its own, because the population moved — a third forced-eval instrument
# (the 90-row maneuver_uniform_v1 leg) joins the census and the mandelbrot floor, and a
# split assignment that only exists as a diff against another file is a split assignment
# nobody can read.
#
# Re-included BY EXACT PATH, not by directory, for the v8 reason: a bare `!/data/v10/`
# would also re-include an accidental in-tree aug_cache/ rebuild.
#   v10's plan.jsonl + cache_manifest.jsonl had negations here (and LFS rules in
#   .gitattributes) until 2026-08-08, when both were deleted: 179 MB of rows that
#   `tools/v10/build_plan.py` reproduces BYTE-IDENTICALLY from data/v10/manifest.jsonl plus
#   v9's committed roster and colormaps (proved by rebuilding over the originals and
#   comparing sha256, 2026-08-08). They were tracked as the only map from a cached tile back
#   to a location; data/v{9,10}/aug_cache was deleted earlier the same day. The pair is
#   bulk() now — deliberately untracked, byte-reproducible, and NOT a RELOCATED_PREFIXES
#   entry, so it resolves in-tree at the same path every reader already opens.
!/data/v10/
/data/v10/*
!/data/v10/manifest.jsonl
!/data/v10/eval_slice.jsonl
!/data/v10/build_metadata.json
!/data/v10/aug_roster.json
!/data/v10/colormaps.json
# v10 EVAL products — the frozen per-location eval slice, the acceptance battery, and the
# pre-registration record written BEFORE any eval ran.
!/data/v10/eval_scores_v10.jsonl
!/data/v10/eval_results_v10.json
!/data/v10/prereg_v10.json
# The ADOPTED discovery t_good table at the v10 flip (tools/v10/derive_t_good_v10.py).
# production_seeder.T_GOOD_OVERRIDES mirrors it and tools/scoring/test_t_good_adoption.py
# holds the two equal, so this file is the derivation half of a live production gate.
!/data/v10/t_good_derivation.json
# Backstop only — the v10 aug cache is bulk() and resolves out-of-tree through
# artifacts.RELOCATED_PREFIXES. If it ever reappears here it stays un-committable.
/data/v10/aug_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v11 classifier build — DURABLE by exact path, and it is ONE path, which is the
# difference from v8/v9/v10 above.
#
# v11's manifest, eval_slice, plan and cache_manifest are all `paths.bulk()`: they are a
# deterministic function of the committed label corpus, `tools/v11/build_{manifest,plan}.py`
# and the seed/config recorded below, so they rebuild rather than being restored, and at
# 11,303 locations x 32 tiles the plan alone is ~140 MB of derived rows. What IS committed
# is the small record that makes them rebuildable and checkable: the seed tag, the recipe
# flags, the realized counts and the gate outcomes.
#
# The bulk half resolves out-of-tree through artifacts.RELOCATED_PREFIXES; the two
# backstops below keep it un-committable if it ever reappears in the tree.
!/data/v11/
/data/v11/*
!/data/v11/build_record.json
!/data/v11/aug_recipe.json
!/data/v11/colormaps.json
# The v11 train/certify records. A negation is a DECLARATION that the file belongs in the
# tree, and tests/test_tracked_artifacts.py holds every declared path to being tracked — so
# each line lands in the commit that lands its file, never ahead of it.
#   `prereg_v11.json` is the whole point of pre-registration: a bar in a committed artifact
# the eval script loads cannot be edited after seeing the results.
!/data/v11/prereg_v11.json
#   `eval_results_v11.json` is that script's verdicts; `eval_scores_v11.jsonl` the frozen
# per-location slice `tools/scoring/eval_slice` resolves IN-TREE, and the one .jsonl under
# data/v11/ that is NOT bulk (artifacts._is_v11_build_rows exempts it by name);
# `eval_canon_record.json` says what the deploy-canonical eval tiles are and how to rebuild
# the 3,273 of them that live out-of-tree.
!/data/v11/eval_results_v11.json
!/data/v11/eval_scores_v11.jsonl
!/data/v11/eval_canon_record.json
# The ADOPTED discovery t_good table at the v11 flip (tools/v11/derive_t_good_v11.py) —
# the derivation half of production_seeder.T_GOOD_OVERRIDES and a member of
# production_pins.COUPLED_ARTIFACTS, so it must be a tracked artifact and not a scratch one.
!/data/v11/t_good_derivation.json
# The v11 flip's own record: the rollback ladder (two rungs, v11 -> v10) and what the
# adoption wrote. Separate from build_record.json because the build adopted nothing.
!/data/v11/adoption_record.json
/data/v11/aug_cache/
/data/v11/eval_canon/
/data/v11/plan.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Classifier weights — DURABLE by exact path, and by NEGATION rather than by force-add.
# Force-adding (`git add -f`) works but leaves no rule saying a file belongs: a fresh clone's
# `git add -A` would not re-add it and nothing would notice. Every version below declares
# itself by exact path, checkable with `git check-ignore --no-index` and picked up by the
# derived canary in tests/test_tracked_artifacts.py (BUILD_PREFIX_RE matches
# data/classifier/v<N>/ too).
#
# The re-include chain has to walk down: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is still excluded, so each level is opened and then re-narrowed. Ordering is load-bearing —
# LAST MATCHING RULE WINS, so every per-version block MUST sit after the
# `/data/classifier/*` re-exclusion (a v10 negation placed earlier was silently undone by it
# on the first attempt).
#
# ================== WEIGHTS RETENTION, SET 2026-08-08 ==================
# TRACKED WEIGHTS = ACTIVE + PREVIOUS, per model family. Everything older or rejected
# de-tracks at the flip (docs/design/storage_classes.md § weights retention). At the v11 flip
# that de-tracked FIVE `.pt` files — v5, v6, v7, v8, v9 — and left the ladder at v11 -> v10.
#
# THE RECORDS STAY AND THE WEIGHTS DO NOT. Each retired version keeps its small
# `config.json` (and `metrics.json` where it has one): those are the RECIPE, they cost a
# kilobyte, and losing them was the real hazard — v5/v6/v7 shipped the .pt and nothing else,
# and `classifier/train_v8.py` names v7's checkpoint config as "the only surviving copy of
# the v7 recipe". `tools/scoring/extract_retired_config.py` lifted all three out before the
# weights left. Emergency copies of the weights themselves sit UNREFERENCED at
# <artifacts>/retired_weights/, verified against the LFS pointer oid; nothing here resolves
# that path, on purpose.
!/data/classifier/
/data/classifier/*
# --- retired heads: RECORDS ONLY, no weight (v5, v6, v7, v8, v9) ---
!/data/classifier/v5/
/data/classifier/v5/*
!/data/classifier/v5/config.json
!/data/classifier/v6/
/data/classifier/v6/*
!/data/classifier/v6/config.json
!/data/classifier/v7/
/data/classifier/v7/*
!/data/classifier/v7/config.json
!/data/classifier/v8/
/data/classifier/v8/*
!/data/classifier/v8/config.json
!/data/classifier/v8/metrics.json
!/data/classifier/v9/
/data/classifier/v9/*
!/data/classifier/v9/config.json
!/data/classifier/v9/metrics.json
# --- the ladder: PREVIOUS (v10) and ACTIVE (v11) — weight + records ---
# model_last.pt is deliberately NOT tracked on either: selection is on best, and a second
# 34 MB LFS object per version buys nothing.
!/data/classifier/v10/
/data/classifier/v10/*
!/data/classifier/v10/model_best.pt
!/data/classifier/v10/config.json
!/data/classifier/v10/metrics.json
!/data/classifier/v11/
/data/classifier/v11/*
!/data/classifier/v11/model_best.pt
!/data/classifier/v11/config.json
!/data/classifier/v11/metrics.json

# Backbone comparison (prompts/backbone_search_v1.md, tools/backbone_search/). MEASUREMENT,
# not a flip: nothing here is pinned, and under ACTIVE+PREVIOUS retention a staged arm's
# weight is not trackable at all. What IS durable is the RECORD — the pre-registration, each
# arm's config/metrics/history/log, the frozen paired eval scores and the results table —
# because it is the only surviving description of runs whose weights are thrown away, and
# re-earning it costs the whole GPU-day again.
!/data/backbone_search/
# The per-arm train.log is NOT tracked: metrics.json already carries every epoch's loss and
# per-cutpoint AP as `history`, so a tracked log is the same rows twice in a form nothing
# reads. It is written beside the weights instead (train_arm.py).
/data/backbone_search/records/**/train.log
# The weights themselves. Registered in artifacts.RELOCATED_PREFIXES so they are born OUT of
# the tree; this line is the belt-and-braces half — without it the `!` above would COMMIT any
# weight that ever landed in-tree, which is exactly the trap /data/atlas/tau_h_rederive names.
/data/backbone_search/arms/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# render-mode ("mining") heads — DURABLE by exact path, same wiring and same reason as
# the v9/v10 classifier block above. v1 was force-added and had no rule saying it belongs;
# it is the LIVE gate (mining_pins.ACTIVE_MINING_CKPT) and its training corpus no longer
# exists, so it is the least reproducible weight in the tree and the least appropriate one
# to leave undeclared. Beside it: the gate lock (the frozen operating point + eval ladder
# the 0.50 release floor is set against) and the adoption report that reads it.
#
# v2's WEIGHT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. It was negated (and LFS-tracked) while it was a
# live candidate; it lost the winner rule on 2026-08-06, and a rejected candidate is not a
# critical final weight — the committed trainer (classifier/train_mining_head_v2.py), the
# committed corpus batch and the recipe recorded in config.json reproduce it per-seed. Its
# RUN RECORD stays tracked (config/metrics/per_seed/report.{md,json}); only the ~10 MB of
# weights, and the per-seed dirs that were always ignored, are working state.
# Wallpaper-quality head (classifier/train_wallpaper_v*.py; the pin is
# tools/wallpaper/wallpaper_pins.HEAD_CKPT). Declared by exact-path negation as of
# 2026-08-08; before that v3's weight and v4's two records were tracked by `git add -f` at
# a gitignored path — the same force-add shape data/classifier/ and data/render_mode_head/
# already closed, and the last two instances of it in the tree.
#
# v3 is the LIVE head and the only weight here: under ACTIVE+PREVIOUS retention v4 was a
# staged candidate that was never adopted, so its weight de-tracked on 2026-08-08 and is
# NOT re-included below. What stays of v4 is the record of what was staged — config.json
# (the recipe) and metrics.json (what it scored) — because that is the reason the rejection
# does not get re-litigated. Its 34 MB weight, the five per-seed dirs, eval_scores.jsonl,
# the eval montage and train.log are working state and stay ignored.
!/data/wallpaper_head/
/data/wallpaper_head/*
!/data/wallpaper_head/v3/
/data/wallpaper_head/v3/*
!/data/wallpaper_head/v3/model_best.pt
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4/
/data/wallpaper_head/v4/*
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4/config.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4/metrics.json
# v4b (the (28) retrain: sheet A folded in, trained from scratch). ADOPTED 2026-08-11
# (prompts/flip_29.md) and it is now ACTIVE, so its WEIGHT is tracked — but the pinned
# weight is SEED 1's, not the top-level `model_best.pt` (which is seed 0, the staged max on
# the (28) pooled eval). The seed was picked on best blind sheet-D AUC>=4, so the negation
# walks into the seed dir: a directory negation here would sweep in the other four seeds'
# 34 MB weights and five eval_scores.jsonl (storage_classes.md, "never a directory
# negation"). v3 stays tracked as PREVIOUS; nothing de-tracked at this flip.
#
# Beside the weight: the flip's own derived records. `volume_match_wallpaper.{json,md}` is
# what the two wallpaper cuts were restated against (protocol §5a) — the first durable
# record the wallpaper head's floors have ever had. `fit_slice_pred.json` and
# `july_slice_pred.json` are the suggestion-cut fit slices' readouts under this head, which
# is what keeps `suggest_tier.derive_{intake_,}cuts()` reproducible without a GPU.
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/
/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/*
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/config.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/metrics.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/per_seed.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/report.md
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/report.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/volume_match_wallpaper.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/volume_match_wallpaper.md
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/fit_slice_pred.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/july_slice_pred.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/adoption_record.json
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/seed_1/
/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/seed_1/*
!/data/wallpaper_head/v4b/seed_1/model_best.pt
# The sheet-D re-verdict (v3 vs v4b on the BLIND minibrot slice). Two files, ~27 KB, and
# they are a RUN RECORD in the same sense as v4b's above: the labels they read are human
# judgement on a population that will never be labeled unanchored twice, so the report is
# the only durable form of what that slice said. `anchoring_price()` already reads v4b's
# report.json as data, which is what a report of this class is for.
!/data/wallpaper_head/sheet_d_reverdict/
/data/wallpaper_head/sheet_d_reverdict/*
!/data/wallpaper_head/sheet_d_reverdict/report.md
!/data/wallpaper_head/sheet_d_reverdict/report.json

!/data/render_mode_head/
/data/render_mode_head/*
!/data/render_mode_head/v1/
/data/render_mode_head/v1/*
!/data/render_mode_head/v1/model_best.pt
!/data/render_mode_head/v1/mining_gate_lock.json
!/data/render_mode_head/v1/mining_gate_lock.md
!/data/render_mode_head/v1/report.md
!/data/render_mode_head/v2/
/data/render_mode_head/v2/*
# The three small records that say what produced v2, and the v1-vs-v2 + calibration report
# that is the run's uploadable deliverable. The weight itself is NOT re-included.
!/data/render_mode_head/v2/config.json
!/data/render_mode_head/v2/metrics.json
!/data/render_mode_head/v2/per_seed.json
!/data/render_mode_head/v2/report.md
!/data/render_mode_head/v2/report.json
